nger than  that one says it's easy to be a hero  when you know you're stronger than your  enemy but what is truly impressive is if  you can stand up to a bad guy who is  clearly stronger than you one feels like  that mentality and zeal to rush in to  help even when you know you're weaker is  what defines a hero he says that Saitama  wants that zeal as well but he  taken away from him because he became so  strong in this sense itemised envious of  people like Moomin rider who bravely  rush into a fight with opponents who are  clearly way stronger than they are  that's right ladies and gentlemen Moomin  rider is the ideal hero that the world  desperately needs back number four  Saitama was purposely made to be  different from other heroes in fact one  came up with Saitama simplistic design  in response to how many cool-looking  heroes there were out there think about  it heroes usually have cool hairstyles  expressions and names but Saitama is  bald has a signature derp face and his  hero name is bald cape the illustrator  of the manga mu data pointed out that  sytem is similar to Goku from Dragon  Ball they both have a detached easygoing  this and when things are looking  hopeless the moment they show up you  know things are going to be okay which  is true enough but one also made one  punch man to be different from Shawn and  like Dragonball instead of focusing on a  character's growth one wanted to see  what happens if the hero starts in peak  condition Goku is constantly being  pushed to get stronger than he was  before  while no one has been able to push  Saitama to even use his current full  power not to mention that Super Saiyan  Goku probably has the coolest hair known  to man I think it is exactly because one  punch man challenges all these  conventions that we love it so much  after all you wouldn't see Batman way  more concerned about losing his wallet  than saving the world fact number 5 you  may already know that mob cycle 101 and  one punch man are both 